  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14284903/assets/35e807b7de787f50d0cbff770e4083cef84b4d35030b4c506b1db5646cf7a358.png)\n\nThe addition law for probability states that\n\n$$\nP(A\\cup B)=P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B).\n$$\n\nSo, to calculate $P(A\\cup B),$ we apply the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\  & =0.45+0.35-0.3 \\\\  & =0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe Venn diagram corresponding to this situation is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14284903/assets/d0e28e43ee4b198cb83eabe168c8fdcd675570361d05a2d2c07e691543fef078.png)",
